#chip mega328p, 16

'Repeat For test (Change 1654): An interrupt handler exists in the program (interrupts are ignored by the calculation) on mega328p
'Expect: compiles, and the whole Repeat For construct runs exactly 8,000 clock cycles
'(checked by simulating the generated assembly instruction by instruction)

#option explicit
Dim Flag As Bit
Dim Cnt As Byte
Dim X As Byte
Dim Y As Byte
Dim W1 As Word
Dim W2 As Word
Dim Ticks As Byte
On Interrupt Timer0Overflow Call Tick
Sub Tick
    Ticks = Ticks + 1
End Sub
Repeat For 500 us
    Wait 10 us
End Repeat
Do
Loop
